WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:07.106
Every app needs its own full Supabase stack. One server carries them all, and it bends.

00:07.800 --> 00:12.853
Sbarbase makes the server one building. Postgres runs once, in the basement.

00:14.600 --> 00:23.369
Each client is a floor, each project an apartment, each environment a window with its own lock and its own database.

00:24.100 --> 00:30.349
Your app speaks Supabase as usual. The gateway sends each request to its own environment.

00:30.500 --> 00:35.042
A request without the right key never gets in.

00:35.800 --> 00:39.576
Every night, each environment is backed up, encrypted, off the server.

00:40.800 --> 00:46.248
If one breaks, only it is restored. The others never notice.

00:48.500 --> 00:51.301
One command installs it all.

00:53.300 --> 00:58.957
Sbarbase. Many Supabase projects, one server.
